<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov jobless rate edges down to 3.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov jobless rate edges down to 3.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's seasonally adjusted unemployment rate in November edged down to 3.3 percent from 3.4 percent in October, the government announced on Friday.</p>
<p>The jobs-to-applicants ratio rose to 0.74 in November from 0.73 in October, it said.</p>
<p>The following  is a breakdown of the jobs data:</p>
<p>    (Adjusted)			November  October   Year ago</p>
<p>    Unemployment rate	     3.3 pct   3.4 pct    3.4 pct</p>
<p>					  November  October   Year ago</p>
<p>    Jobs-to-applicants ratio    0.74	0.73	  0.63</p>
<p> (Unadjusted)		    November  October     Year ago</p>
<p> Unemployment rate	     3.2 pct   3.4 pct     3.3 pct</p>
<p> Number of unemployed	  2.12 million  2.27 million    2.18 million</p>
<p> Number of employed		  November     Year/year change</p>
<p> Overall				 64.97 million    +0.9 pct</p>
<p>Main Industries:</p>
<p>  Manufacturing			14.49 million    -0.9 pct</p>
<p>  Services			     15.93 million    +2.8 pct</p>
<p>  Wholesale, retail, restaurants 14.80 million    +1.2 pct</p>
<p>  Construction			  6.90 million    +1.9 pct</p>
<p>  Agriculture			   3.17 million    -0.9 pct</p>
</text>
